<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xin dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9–23</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Xin dynasty was the short-lived regime of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-mang">Wang Mang</a>, who usurped the throne of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> in 9 CE and proclaimed a &quot;new&quot; (xin) dynasty. His reforms, including the nationalisation of land, a ban on the sale of slaves and repeated changes of currency, caused disorder, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> floods and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-eyebrows">Red Eyebrows</a> rebellion spread revolt. Wang Mang was killed when rebels took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> in 23, and the Han was restored under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-guangwu-of-han">Emperor Guangwu</a> in 25.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xin-dynasty.jpg" alt="Xin dynasty" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SS · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Xin_Dynasty.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
